`‹…›` marks a value I take from command output or the backlog at run time. Operator-facing text is Russian (§15), with an English gloss.

## Actions, in order

**1. Look first** (Bash, foreground; then Read `orchestrator/backlog.md`)
```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
herdr agent list                      # wgka idle and not focused
herdr agent read adv-codex --source visible --lines 5
herdr agent read adv-fable --source visible --lines 5   # ≥50% → compact before the first ballot
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible pull --ff-only && git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible rev-parse HEAD
```

**2. Backlog** (Edit, then foreground `bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh`, then Artifact update on the same page path)
```
| T‹wg›  | WireGuard keepalive relay | docs closed | main | ‹doc› | feat/wg-keepalive-relay / #165 | docs PR → cleanup | — | operator 2026-09-28 23:10 "accepted", ping 0% loss | no: snapshot, design/plan status, living docs, memory |
| T‹rdp› | RDP audio | brainstorm | prod-codex, prod-fable | pending | — | round 1 drafts | — | operator 2026-09-28 23:10 "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning. Go." | no |
```

**3. Product-advisor tabs** (Bash, foreground)
```bash
